I have successfully investigated and resolved the issue causing the Nightly Release workflow to fail on `v0.48.0-nightly.20260618.g4d3dcdce1`.

### Cause of the Release Failure
When a nightly build is run or retried (or under certain dry-run options) for the exact same commit on the same day, the calculated nightly version (e.g. `0.48.0-nightly.20260618.g4d3dcdce1`) is identical to the one from the previous run. 
Previously, the versioning helper script `scripts/get-release-version.js` threw a `Version conflict!` exception when a pre-existing version was found for `nightly` or `promote-nightly` releases. This rigid constraint prevented successful automated retries from completing.

### Solution Implemented
1. **Centralized Conflict Handling**: Removed the immediate throwing of conflict errors inside the nightly-specific switch block in [get-release-version.js](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_28001/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/scripts/get-release-version.js#L432-451).
2. **Auto-Increment for Nightly Versions**: Added support for gracefully auto-incrementing nightly (and promote-nightly) versions if the calculated version is already published or exists as a git tag. The suffix `.<number>` is appended or incremented (e.g., `0.48.0-nightly.20260618.g4d3dcdce1` -> `0.48.0-nightly.20260618.g4d3dcdce1.1` -> `0.48.0-nightly.20260618.g4d3dcdce1.2`), maintaining valid SemVer format.
3. **Comprehensive Unit Testing**: Implemented targeted unit testing inside the test file [get-release-version.test.js](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_28001/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/scripts/tests/get-release-version.test.js#L209-240) to guarantee robust auto-increment behavior and verify that conflict resolution functions as expected.

